WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.013
Learn to use an understanding of one-to-one correspondence to read and interpret

00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:09.826
graphs and use an understanding of many-to-one correspondence to display or construct

00:00:09.826 --> 00:00:10.227
graphs

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:16.748
In a chart, one picture means one pupil. There are 7 orange pictures. How many pupils

00:00:16.748 --> 00:00:20.676
chose orange? The answer is 7. One symbol represents one pupil.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:26.653
A pictograph uses one picture for one pupil. There are 17 pictures of mangoes. How

00:00:26.653 --> 00:00:30.749
many pupils chose them? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:35.329
The answer is 17. Each symbol represents one pupil.
